      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the code. Let me write an improved version with better naming, a descriptive comment on the helper method, and clearer variable names to make the test more understandable.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were:\n\n- Renamed `trackSeen` → `appendNodeLabel` (better describes what the method does: appends a label, not just tracks)\n- Added a Javadoc comment to `appendNodeLabel` explaining the label format for each node type\n- Renamed local variable `seen` → `visitedElements` (clarifies that these are only elements, not all node types)\n- Added a comment on the html field describing its structure\n- Added an inline comment explaining that `NodeIterator<Element>` skips non-element nodes\n- Added a comment above the assertion spelling out the expected traversal path in plain English"
